course: dictionary
lesson: 3663
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fissure is a long, narrow crack, especially in rock or the ground. Picture a thin crack running along a pavement or down the side of a cliff.
explain: A fissure can also be a natural groove in the body, or a small painful crack in the skin. It can even mean a split between people in a group. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Look at this context: «Fissure sealants are thin plastic coatings painted into the grooves of back teeth to keep food and bacteria out, but they don't replace brushing.» Coatings and grooves are the clues. Try the rock meaning in the sentence and it fails. Try the groove meaning and it makes sense.
fact: A fissure is a long, narrow crack.
fact: «A fissure in the rock» means a crack in the rock.
fact: «Volcanic fissure» means a crack in the ground where lava can come out.
fact: In the body, a fissure can be a natural groove, such as a fold in the brain, or a small painful crack in the skin.
fact: Fissure sealants are thin plastic coatings that fill the grooves of back teeth, but they don't replace brushing.
exercise: What is a fissure in the rock? | A deep, cold lake | *A long, narrow crack | A hard, shiny stone | A pile of loose sand
exercise: In «Fissure sealants are thin plastic coatings painted into the grooves of back teeth», where are the sealants painted? | Under the ground | *Into the grooves of back teeth | On the top of the skin | Onto the rock of a volcano
exercise: A fissure can mean a split between people in a group. What does that tell us? | It means a soft, warm song | *It can mean a disagreement that splits people apart | It means a fast game played outdoors | It means a party with lots of music
test: What can come out of a volcanic fissure? | Feathers | *Lava | Snow | Sand from the beach
test: In the body, which of these is a fissure? | *A small painful crack in the skin | A loud drum beat | A tall, green tree | A cold glass of water
exam: In «Fissure sealants are thin plastic coatings painted into the grooves of back teeth», which meaning of fissure fits? | A long river flowing to the sea | A crack in a mountain of rock | *A narrow groove in a tooth | A split between friends in a team
